[{"id":3549250577,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7TjUQR","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"ea88db898c3f1c1196472af83a01cfb24201177b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","login":"deralmas","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas"},"body":"Hi, here's what I think. Note that most of my code proposals come from my first impressions, you might need to experiment.\n\nThere are two big things that I identified:\n\n - I'm curious about the pressure & tilt emulation. I have some trouble understanding it (I don't know touch screens very well) and personally I think that it'd be safer to go without them.\n\n - While it might work, _technically_ we need to do the \"frame\" thing, which is even more annoying since we have multiple touch points.\n\nIf you need any help, feel free to ask :D\n\nAs luck would have it, yesterday I set up a touch emulator (again), so now I can also make changes that are not \"blind\", if that helps.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113705#pullrequestreview-3549250577","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113705","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-12-07T13:08:33Z"},{"id":3549307025,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7TjiCR","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"ea88db898c3f1c1196472af83a01cfb24201177b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69566148?u=5e6f5ad1955c17ad8bc2fc454a52fa1719e5bbe9&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/laomengwa","id":69566148,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NTY